/* Dead Signal — packs/ds-story/levels/f3-gestation.js
 * Floor 3, Gestation (DESIGN.md section 4.3): where the specimens are grown. A ring of corridor round
 * the vat hall, restricted labs off it (each with its own horror, most in containment, some not), the
 * partners' briefing suite where it was all called "macroscopic synthids", and a Director on the
 * intercom who badly wants you not to look.
 *
 * The route: Stair A (foamed shut above; Voss: straight across to Stair B, don't stop) → Stair B's door
 * wants Level 3 clearance; Brandt keeps a spare in her office (toBrandt) → round the east corridor (keep
 * to it) to Dr. Brandt's office: her terminal says Okafor took the spare and his card has been read in
 * Lab 3-B every thirty-one minutes all night (knowsOkafor) → Lab 3-B: Okafor is up and walking, ridden
 * by a Tenant; put him down and take the card (clearance3) → back to Stair B. On the landing, Voss makes
 * his case, and what he says depends on what you've seen (sawSpecimen, the file flags, fileColony); the
 * stairs wait until he's done (vossDone).
 * Off the route: Lab 3-A (the Midwife: eggs; cell 3 breaks when you go to the back), Lab 3-D (Lanterns in
 * the dark), Lab 3-E (juvenile Congregations in pens; Colony 4 went to Shelter B), Cell S-41 (empty;
 * transferred to Five), the vat hall and its Sitter (another walks the ring), the briefing suite, the
 * pump room (the Plasma Cutter; breaker 3P powers ARIADNE's relay: three more Orderlies, and the east
 * turret, on your side), ARIADNE's relay itself (its standing orders; fragment 6).
 * The robots in defence mode and the specimens fight each other on this floor (the level's factions).
 *
 * Generated from a layout script, then meant to be tuned in the editor. Two layers: map (terrain,
 * keyed by legend) and objects (furniture, people and props, keyed by objectLegend).
 */
